alReport/532440/5324400315.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"2014-03-31","title":"Financial Year 2014","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532440/5324400314.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"2013-03-31","title":"Financial Year 2013","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532440/5324400313.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"2012-03-31","title":"Financial Year 2012","url":"https://archives.nseindia.com/annual_reports/AR_MPSLTD_2011_2012_31122012122020.zip","source":"screener"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"2012-03-31","title":"Financial Year 2012","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532440/5324400312.pdf","source":"bse"}],"analysis":{"summary":"MPS Limited reported its strongest opening quarter for Q1 FY27, achieving record revenue, EBITDA, and PAT, and positioning the company as a Rule of 50 company. Management reiterated its FY27 EBITDA guidance to comfortably cross INR 300 crores, supported by strong performance across research, education, and corporate learning segments. The company also highlighted improved operating leverage, disciplined resource management, and increased client diversification driven by the integration of Unbound Medicine. Management reported that FY26 was the most profitable year in the company's history, driven by strong performance across research and education segments alongside structural recovery in corporate learning. The company expects to comfortably exceed INR 300 crores in EBITDA in FY27 based on bottom-up operating plans and current run rates.","themes":{"guidance":[{"claim":"Management reiterated the FY27 EBITDA guidance of comfortably crossing INR 300 crores.","quote":"FY27: TRACKING TO COMFORTBALY CROSS INR 300 CRORES IN EBITDA\nINR 300+ Cr\nFY27 EBITDA GUIDANCE, REITERATED\n~21% three-year EBITDA CAGR (FY24 to FY27), built bottom-up from each segment operating plan","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=0f2c9a6d-7a46-44ae-a149-b68925f2e76b.pdf"},{"claim":"Management stated that the company is positioned to comfortably clear the INR 300 Crores EBITDA mark.","quote":"Q1 landed ahead of a straight-line path, and our second half has historically outrun our first. We continue to regard INR 300 Crores as a mark we are positioned to clear comfortably.","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=0f2c9a6d-7a46-44ae-a149-b68925f2e76b.pdf"}],"demand_outlook":[{"claim":"Growth in Corporate Learning is broadening across geographies, with new client additions, and AI and technology-led engagements.","quote":"Growth is broadening across geographies, with new client additions, and AI and technology-led engagements","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=0f2c9a6d-7a46-44ae-a149-b68925f2e76b.pdf"},{"claim":"The demand for trusted AI deployment inside high-stakes knowledge workflows is expanding sharply.","quote":"On the other side, the demand for what we call trusted AI deployment inside high-stakes knowledge workflows, so think of medicine, nursing, scholarly publishing, regulated learning accessibility, there the demand is going to expand sharply.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"}],"capex_expansion":[{"claim":"Unbound Medicine acquisition closed on February 9, 2026.","quote":"Third, the Unbound Medicine acquisition, which closed on February 9, 2026.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"}],"margins_costs":[{"claim":"Education headcount reduced 4.26% YoY to 765, reflecting disciplined resource management even as revenue scaled.","quote":"Headcount reduced 4.26% YoY to 765, reflecting disciplined resource management even as revenue scaled","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=0f2c9a6d-7a46-44ae-a149-b68925f2e76b.pdf"},{"claim":"Leaner headcount in Corporate Learning unlocked operating leverage, expanding EBITDA margins to 25.33% and EBITDA by 60.69% YoY.","quote":"Leaner headcount unlocked operating leverage, expanding EBITDA margins to 25.33% and EBITDA by 60.69% YoY","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=0f2c9a6d-7a46-44ae-a149-b68925f2e76b.pdf"},{"claim":"Group revenue for the year was INR 768 crores, up by 5.7% over FY25, with EBITDA expanding to 30.7%.","quote":"Group revenue for the year was INR 768 crores, up by 5.7% over FY\u201925. EBITDA was INR 236 crores, up by 11.8%, with the EBITDA margin expanding to 30.7%.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"},{"claim":"Q4 revenue grew 12.7% year-over-year to INR 205 crores and EBITDA grew 20.5% to INR 67.5 crores.","quote":"Q4 specifically was the strongest quarter for FY\u201926. Revenue grew 12.7% year-over-year to INR 205 crores. EBITDA grew 20.5% to INR 67.5 crores with the margins expanding to 32.9%, indicating operating leverage at work as revenue growth converted to margin expansion.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"}],"orders_capacity":[{"claim":"Client diversification stepped up structurally with 841 clients billed in Q1 FY27 compared to 404 a year ago.","quote":"Client diversification stepped up structurally: 841 clients billed in Q1 FY27 vs 404 a year ago, driven by Unbound Medicine's institutional subscriber base being added to our portfolio","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=0f2c9a6d-7a46-44ae-a149-b68925f2e76b.pdf"},{"claim":"Corporate learning closed Q4 with the strongest order book of FY26.","quote":"Q4 closed with the strongest order book of FY'26.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"}],"capital_allocation":[{"claim":"Debtors DSO improved QoQ to 45 days from 51 days, reflecting enhanced collection efficiency and tighter working capital management.","quote":"DSO improved QoQ to 45 days from 51 days, reflecting enhanced collection efficiency and tighter working capital management","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=0f2c9a6d-7a46-44ae-a149-b68925f2e76b.pdf"},{"claim":"Total cash and cash equivalents stood at INR 113.75 crores as of 31 March 2026, with borrowings of INR 40.25 crores for Unbound Medicine.","quote":"On the balance sheet, total cash and cash equivalents stood at INR 113.75 crores as of 31 March 26, with borrowings of INR 40.25 crores relating to the facility drawn for the acquisition of Unbound Medicine.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"},{"claim":"The Board chose not to recommend a final dividend for FY26 due to capital deployment into the Unbound Medicine acquisition and an active M&A pipeline.","quote":"Over FY\u201926, the Board has chosen not to recommend a final dividend. The reason is straightforward. We've deployed capital into the Unbound Medicine acquisition in February, we're carrying a hyperactive M&A pipeline, and the deployment opportunity in front of us exceeds the cash in hand.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"},{"claim":"Total cash and cash equivalents as on March 31, 2026 stood at INR 11,375 Lakhs, while borrowings outstanding were INR 4,025 Lakhs.","quote":"Total cash and cash equivalents as on 31-Mar-2026 stood at INR 11,375 Lakhs, while borrowings outstanding as of 31-Mar-2026 were INR 4,025 Lakhs","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=e7cea350-fc15-4b56-946d-59b7bf9d7ffd.pdf"},{"claim":"Total CSR spending at a consolidated level is INR 300 Lakhs for FY26.","quote":"TOTAL CSR SPENDING AT A CONSOLIDATED LEVEL IS INR 300 LAKHS FOR FY26","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=e7cea350-fc15-4b56-946d-59b7bf9d7ffd.pdf"}],"risks_headwinds":[]},"management_commitments":[{"claim":"Management reiterated FY27 EBITDA guidance to comfortably cross INR 300 crores.","quote":"FY27: TRACKING TO COMFORTBALY CROSS INR 300 CRORES IN EBITDA\nINR 300+ Cr\nFY27 EBITDA GUIDANCE, REITERATED\n~21% three-year EBITDA CAGR (FY24 to FY27), built bottom-up from each segment operating plan","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=0f2c9a6d-7a46-44ae-a149-b68925f2e76b.pdf","timeframe":"FY27"},{"claim":"Management targets INR 300+ Cr in EBITDA by FY27.","quote":"Targeting INR 300+ Cr by FY27 from INR 79 Cr in FY20","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=e7cea350-fc15-4b56-946d-59b7bf9d7ffd.pdf","timeframe":"FY27"}],"coverage":{"docs_analysed":3,"kinds":["concall_ppt","concall_transcript"]}},"_meta":{"model":"gemini-3.6-flash","grounded":true,"facts_kept":18,"facts_dropped_ungrounded":18,"note":"Facts are verbatim-grounded against the company's own documents; claims whose quote was not found were dropped."}}